This page is for having a public resource for documenting Meshtastic activity in Bloomington.

== What is Meshtastic? ==
[https://meshtastic.org https://meshtastic.org]

=== What does it do?===
* Allows texting and GPS position reporting
* Provides a low-speed telemetry communication channel (speeds vary, but 1kb/s is average)
* Excellent for off-grid communication and emergency communication (texting, gps, weather data, other sensor data)

=== What are the parts of the system?===
* An open LoRA mesh protocol specification (in the US, primarily running in the 900MHz ISM band)
* Low power means license free operation (part15 in US)
* LoRA long distance radio - 1-2km at ground level
 
* A collection of low-cost hardware devices by different vendors that implement the protocol
* An app for Android and iPhone that communicates with the hardware

=== Why is it interesting?===
* Works in dead zones (wilderness, marine, etc) and works when cell networks are down
* Low power and long distance - 1-2 miles at ground level, can go hundreds of miles with high elevation line-of-sight
* Meshing capability means the more nodes that are in range of each other extends the overall range of the network in the local area

== Bloomington Coverage ==
There are several nodes placed around Bloomington that provide good high-altitude wide-area coverage:
* IMU
* CIB
* Bloominglabs

